hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16055","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, he said, my father informed me, from Abd Allah ibn Arqam, that he performed pilgrimage, and he would pray with his companions, calling adhan and iqamah, and one day he held the prayer, and said, let one of you pray, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When one of you intends to go to the privy, and the prayer is established, let him go to the privy."
"16514","He said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Hisham, he said: My father narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Arqam, that he went out from Makkah, and he used to lead them in prayer, and call the adhan and the iqamah, so one day he established the prayer, then he said: Let a man among you lead you in prayer, for indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: When one of you wants to go to relieve himself and the prayer is established, then let him go to relieve himself."
